psi_descent.v gets OOM-killed even with a 64GB cgroup limit.
Observed peak: rocqworker used ~63GB RSS (`anon-rss:66489324kB`) before being killed at the 64GB job boundary (2026-04-20).
Need `--mem=128G` (or more) in Slurm job allocation.

psi_cdindex.v (1950 LOC, depends on psi_descent.v) likely has similar requirements — not yet tested.

**Why:** The cgroup at `/sys/fs/cgroup/.../job_NNNN/memory.max` caps RSS regardless of node capacity. The node (mem001, partition=mem) has 3TB but only gives what's requested. Previous estimate of 32GB was too low.

**How to apply:** If coqc/rocqworker gets SIGKILL (exit 137), check `dmesg | tail` for `oom-kill` and the cgroup limit before debugging the proof. Use `salloc --partition=mem --mem=128G --time=48:00:00 --job-name=coq`.
